# Tests that need a capability a bare GitHub runner does not have.
#
# M17.5 F-79: the CI `test` job installed rustup and cargo-nextest, then ran the
# whole workspace on three operating systems. The suite needs pandoc, a nightly
# toolchain with cargo-fuzz, strace, a writable /var/tmp sanitizer build root and
# a reachable crates.io. Every push run on main failed from at least 2026-09-11,
# so the signal was constant and nobody read it.
#
# This file is the ONE place the split is written. CI runs this expression in a
# job that installs the tools, and its negation everywhere else, so the two sides
# are complements by construction rather than by assertion. Adding a test that
# needs a capability means adding it here; forgetting puts it in the portable job
# where it FAILS rather than silently skipping, which is the outcome this project
# wants from a missing capability.
#
# Names are EXACT. A prefix pattern would drag in neighbours that need nothing --
# most haq::tests::canary_* are pure logic -- and quietly drop them from the
# cross-platform job, which is coverage lost for no reason.
#
# Derived from the ubuntu-latest failures of run 35472022586. macOS and Windows
# may need more; the partition check names what moved, and the portable job
# fails loudly rather than skipping, so a missing entry is visible.
#
# scripts/check_ci_partition.sh proves the split covers the suite exactly.
test(=haq::tests::sanitizer_replay_reproduces_the_canonical_build_and_refuses_the_rest)
+ test(=haq::tests::canary_evidence_must_match_a_replay_from_the_fixed_commit)
+ test(=haq::tests::canary_runner_rejects_prose_that_misdescribes_its_own_mutation)
+ test(=haq::tests::concurrency_evidence_is_read_from_disk_not_assumed)
+ test(=haq::tests::corpus_access_audit_rejects_forbidden_paths_and_accepts_unlocked_paths)
+ test(=vstd_admission::tests::current_workspace_metadata_is_admitted)
+ test(=conversion_loss::pandoc_roundtrip_loss_matches_golden)
+ test(=m10::pandoc_version_pinned)
+ test(=m10::declared_level_matches_loss_report)
+ test(=one_projection_reaches_canonical_roundtrip_and_lenses_are_measured)
+ test(=projection_laws_and_identity_ceilings_are_frozen)
+ test(=real_cst_anchor_recovery_report_matches_golden)
